# Tool crash isolation

```elixir
Mix.install([{:elixir_harness, path: "."}])
```

A crashing tool returns `{:error, _}`. The session survives.

```elixir
defmodule Boom do
  use ElixirHarness.Tool
  tool_name("boom")
  tool_description("Raises.")
  tool_schema(%{})
  @impl true
  def run(_), do: raise("boom")
end

{:ok, session} = ElixirHarness.Session.start_link()
ElixirHarness.ToolRunner.run(Boom, %{}) |> IO.inspect(label: "crash")
ElixirHarness.ToolRunner.run(ElixirHarness.Tools.Math, %{"op" => "add", "a" => 1, "b" => 2})
|> IO.inspect(label: "session survives")
```

Why Elixir: `Task.Supervisor` + `Task.yield` gives timeout/kill with no
retry library. Let-it-crash applies to tools, not sessions.
